{title: Will the Circle Be Unbroken}
{artist: Traditional}
{key: G}

{c: Verse 1}
I was [G]standing by my window, on one [C]cold and cloudy [G]day,
When I saw the hearse come rolling, for to [D]carry my mother a[G]way.

{c: Chorus}
Will the [G]circle be un[G7]broken, by and [C]by, Lord, by and [G]by?
There's a better home a-waiting, in the [D]sky, Lord, in the [G]sky.

{c: Verse 2}
[G]Lord, I told the undertaker, "Under[C]taker, please drive [G]slow,
For this body you are hauling, Lord, I [D]hate to see her [G]go."
